WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.242
Today we present a platform that makes our university's examinations secure,

2
00:00:05.242 --> 00:00:06.526
fast and fully digital.

3
00:00:06.846 --> 00:00:11.490
A U T Secure Exam, designed and built here at Ajou University in Tashkent.

4
00:00:13.617 --> 00:00:17.978
Examinations are one of the most demanding processes in any university:

5
00:00:17.978 --> 00:00:21.233
slow to organise, costly to run, and hard to protect.

6
00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:28.586
Paper exams need printing, rooms and invigilators, and every sheet is marked by hand.

7
00:00:28.906 --> 00:00:33.504
In programming courses, professors run student code one submission at a time.

8
00:00:34.317 --> 00:00:38.276
Generic quiz tools do not secure the student's device and cannot run code.

9
00:00:38.596 --> 00:00:42.659
Commercial proctoring charges per student, and often stores data abroad.

10
00:00:43.483 --> 00:00:48.278
The result: days of manual work, and records scattered across paper and spreadsheets.

11
00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:53.673
Our answer is one platform for the whole examination cycle,

12
00:00:53.673 --> 00:00:58.190
from creating an exam to publishing results, on the computers and phones students

13
00:00:58.190 --> 00:00:58.859
already use.

14
00:01:00.983 --> 00:01:04.594
Students take exams in a secure Windows or Android app.

15
00:01:04.914 --> 00:01:09.736
Multiple choice is marked instantly, and programs are run against the professor's test

16
00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:13.772
cases in an isolated sandbox, while professors watch every student live.

17
00:01:14.583 --> 00:01:18.554
Every answer is saved the moment it changes, even through network drops.

18
00:01:18.874 --> 00:01:24.396
Everything is managed centrally, and the platform also offers I E L T S style English

19
00:01:24.396 --> 00:01:24.981
practice.

20
00:01:27.083 --> 00:01:30.160
We built it with modern, mostly open-source technology.

21
00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:35.019
The apps use Electron for Windows, and Kotlin with Jetpack Compose for Android.

22
00:01:35.339 --> 00:01:38.062
The server runs on Node dot J S with Express, secured with J S O N Web Tokens and

23
00:01:38.062 --> 00:01:38.869
scrypt password hashing.

24
00:01:39.683 --> 00:01:42.725
Data is stored in S Q Lite with hourly backups.

25
00:01:43.045 --> 00:01:49.860
Programs run in Judge0, an isolated Docker sandbox, for Python, Java and C plus plus.

26
00:01:50.683 --> 00:01:54.956
It is deployed on Ubuntu Linux behind nginx with H T T P S.

27
00:01:55.276 --> 00:01:58.573
For English, speech is transcribed on our own server with Whisper.

28
00:02:00.683 --> 00:02:05.993
Students and professors connect over a secure H T T P S address on the university's

29
00:02:05.993 --> 00:02:06.953
own sub-domain.

30
00:02:07.783 --> 00:02:11.127
One exam server holds every account, exam and answer,

31
00:02:11.127 --> 00:02:14.030
while student code runs in a separate sandbox.

32
00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:19.067
The interface is clean, branded for our university,

33
00:02:19.067 --> 00:02:22.270
and the same on every device: one home screen for exams,

34
00:02:22.270 --> 00:02:24.672
English practice and the professor portal.

35
00:02:26.783 --> 00:02:28.444
Let us walk through a complete exam.

36
00:02:28.764 --> 00:02:33.082
A professor signs in to the web portal and sees every exam at a glance.

37
00:02:35.183 --> 00:02:39.527
Creating an exam takes minutes: duration, opening and closing time,

38
00:02:39.527 --> 00:02:41.731
allowed apps, and integrity rules.

39
00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:45.487
Questions can be multiple choice, written or programming.

40
00:02:45.807 --> 00:02:50.475
For programs, the professor adds test cases with marks, some visible and some hidden.

41
00:02:52.583 --> 00:02:57.320
Students join with a short access code, or the professor adds a whole class at once.

42
00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:00.657
Now the student's side.

43
00:03:00.977 --> 00:03:04.693
Students sign in, and see their exams with status and schedule.

44
00:03:06.817 --> 00:03:10.088
When the exam starts, the Windows app locks the full screen,

45
00:03:10.088 --> 00:03:11.832
and the Android app pins itself.

46
00:03:12.152 --> 00:03:15.705
Leaving the exam or pasting from outside is recorded.

47
00:03:17.817 --> 00:03:21.350
The timer runs on the server, so closing the app never stops it,

48
00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:23.668
and every answer is saved within a second.

49
00:03:24.483 --> 00:03:28.303
For programming tasks, students run the sample tests before submitting.

50
00:03:30.417 --> 00:03:33.455
Meanwhile, the professor follows every student live:

51
00:03:33.455 --> 00:03:36.260
time left, last activity and integrity warnings,

52
00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:39.298
and can reopen an attempt after a technical problem.

53
00:03:41.417 --> 00:03:45.978
The student submits; if time runs out, the exam is submitted automatically with every

54
00:03:45.978 --> 00:03:46.676
saved answer.

55
00:03:48.783 --> 00:03:51.419
After submission, marking starts automatically.

56
00:03:51.739 --> 00:03:55.454
Each program is run against every test case in the sandbox.

57
00:03:56.283 --> 00:03:59.297
Each passed test earns its marks: four of five pass,

58
00:03:59.297 --> 00:04:02.311
so this student scores eight out of ten, in seconds,

59
00:04:02.311 --> 00:04:03.702
and fairly for everyone.

60
00:04:05.817 --> 00:04:09.423
The professor reviews results in one table, marks written answers,

61
00:04:09.423 --> 00:04:10.844
and exports a spreadsheet.

62
00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:15.960
With one click, results are released, and each student sees only their own marks and

63
00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:16.422
feedback.

64
00:04:18.550 --> 00:04:21.676
The platform also prepares students for I E L T S,

65
00:04:21.676 --> 00:04:24.615
in all four skills and three difficulty levels,

66
00:04:24.615 --> 00:04:26.178
with instant band scores.

67
00:04:28.283 --> 00:04:31.836
Security is built into every layer: role-based access,

68
00:04:31.836 --> 00:04:36.178
strongly hashed passwords, account locking, and encrypted traffic.

69
00:04:36.983 --> 00:04:40.351
Student code is isolated, every important action is logged,

70
00:04:40.351 --> 00:04:43.775
and the database is backed up hourly, with a tested restore.

71
00:04:45.883 --> 00:04:49.101
For our university, the benefits are direct: lower costs,

72
00:04:49.101 --> 00:04:53.221
with no printing and no per-student licences, and much faster evaluation.

73
00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:57.754
Exams and results are managed centrally, with stronger integrity.

74
00:04:58.583 --> 00:05:01.949
It scales to large classes, and makes better use of our labs,

75
00:05:01.949 --> 00:05:04.156
students' devices, and professors' time.

76
00:05:06.283 --> 00:05:10.916
We also tested it under load, simulating students exactly as the apps behave.

77
00:05:11.236 --> 00:05:13.964
The first version handled two hundred and fifty students.

78
00:05:14.783 --> 00:05:19.532
After optimisation, a single laptop handled seven hundred and fifty students signing

79
00:05:19.532 --> 00:05:24.224
in at the same moment, and one thousand five hundred taking an exam simultaneously,

80
00:05:24.224 --> 00:05:26.033
with responses under one second.

81
00:05:28.150 --> 00:05:30.632
Most importantly, not a single answer was lost:

82
00:05:30.632 --> 00:05:33.537
more than ninety four thousand were checked one by one.

83
00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:36.881
We even crashed the server in the middle of an exam.

84
00:05:37.201 --> 00:05:39.662
After the restart, every answer was still there.

85
00:05:41.783 --> 00:05:45.712
Looking ahead, the platform can serve other universities in Uzbekistan,

86
00:05:45.712 --> 00:05:47.704
and connect with learning platforms.

87
00:05:48.024 --> 00:05:49.975
These are next steps, not yet built.

88
00:05:50.783 --> 00:05:54.148
Natural extensions include Uzbek and Russian interfaces,

89
00:05:54.148 --> 00:05:56.612
and analytics with shared question banks.

90
00:05:57.417 --> 00:06:02.008
With A I assisted marking, A U T Secure Exam can grow from a university project into a

91
00:06:02.008 --> 00:06:02.862
startup product.

92
00:06:04.983 --> 00:06:06.760
The system is built and tested.

93
00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:11.178
Next is installation on the university server, at exam dot ajou dot u z.

94
00:06:11.983 --> 00:06:16.762
After a pilot with one class, real examinations can begin about four weeks after the

95
00:06:16.762 --> 00:06:17.672
server is ready.

96
00:06:18.483 --> 00:06:21.374
Then, all faculties, and partner universities.

97
00:06:23.483 --> 00:06:27.515
A U T Secure Exam shows what our university can build for itself:

98
00:06:27.515 --> 00:06:32.850
secure, fair and efficient examinations, and a real step in the digital transformation

99
00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:34.524
of education in Uzbekistan.

100
00:06:36.650 --> 00:06:38.171
We are ready to begin the pilot.

101
00:06:38.491 --> 00:06:38.920
Thank you.
